  "term": "DIF",
  "definition": "In assessment, DIF stands for differential item functioning, a method for examining whether a test item functions differently for two groups after controlling for their ability level. It is used to detect potential item or test bias and to flag items for further review, but DIF findings alone do not necessarily demonstrate bias.",
